# Line endings fixed per file type, whatever core.autocrlf says on the attendee's machine. Text is LF: the
# files are read by Bash, awk, Docker and Hugo in Linux containers, which take a CRLF as part of the text
# (a shell script fails, a front matter is not found, a value ends with \r). Windows scripts keep CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.jar binary
